[meta] Link Relations Demo
This file exercises all 20 EMD link relation types.

## [example|done] Depends Relation
A link showing a dependency on another file.
→ depends: all-types.emd

## [example|done] Blocks Relation
This task blocks progress on another item.
→ blocks: tasks.emd

## [example|done] Related Relation
This is related to another document.
→ related: project.emd

## [example|done] Requires Relation
This requirement must be fulfilled first.
→ requires: api-spec.emd

## [example|done] Follows Relation
This follows another task in sequence.
→ follows: decisions.emd

## [example|done] Precedes Relation
This comes before another item.
→ precedes: bug-tracker.emd

## [example|done] Extends Relation
This extends an existing specification.
→ extends: spec.emd

## [example|done] Implements Relation
The implementation of a specification.
→ implements: schema.emd

## [example|done] Defines Relation
This defines an interface or contract.
→ defines: config.emd

## [example|done] References Relation
This references external documentation.
→ references: template.emd

## [example|done] Contains Relation
This document contains other elements.
→ contains: nested.emd

## [example|done] Supersedes Relation
This replaces an older version.
→ supersedes: log.emd

## [example|done] Conflicts Relation
This has a known conflict with another item.
→ conflicts: api.emd

## [example|done] Mirrors Relation
This mirrors content from another source.
→ mirrors: memory.emd

## [example|done] Splits Relation
This splits from an existing item.
→ splits: summary.emd

## [example|done] Merges Relation
This merges multiple items together.
→ merges: detail.emd

## [example|done] Generates Relation
This produces output consumed elsewhere.
→ generates: prompt.emd

## [example|done] Consumes Relation
This consumes output from another source.
→ consumes: model.emd

## [example|done] Wiki Links
Testing [[wiki-link]] syntax and [[another-page]] navigation.
See [[all-types]] and [[project]] for more context.
